    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0160" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2434</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-13T13:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1916, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Official statement reported given out in Japan to the effect that foreigners in
                    China desire more protection has no foundation. Conditions <pb facs="0161"
                        n="85" xml:id="pg85"/> here are again perfectly normal, with no apprehension
                    on the part of foreigners and with a feeling of confidence in assured
                    realization of economic political progress under the Republic.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
